{"id":"mahabharata-3-105","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":105,"title":"पञ्चाधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 105 · The sacrificial horse disappears","summary":{"en":"Sagara's sixty thousand sons are born from a gourd and grow up wild and violent. When Sagara performs the horse sacrifice, the horse vanishes; the sons dig the earth in search of it and find it near the sage Kapila.","kn":"ಸಗರನ ಅರವತ್ತು ಸಾವಿರ ಮಕ್ಕಳು ಸೋರೆಕಾಯಿಯಿಂದ ಹುಟ್ಟಿ ಉದ್ಧಟರಾಗಿ ಬೆಳೆಯುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಸಗರನು ಅಶ್ವಮೇಧ ಮಾಡುವಾಗ ಕುದುರೆ ಮಾಯವಾಗುತ್ತದೆ; ಮಕ್ಕಳು ಅದಕ್ಕಾಗಿ ಭೂಮಿಯನ್ನು ಅಗೆದು ಕಪಿಲ ಋಷಿಯ ಬಳಿ ಅದನ್ನು ಕಾಣುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"सगर के साठ हज़ार पुत्र एक तुम्बी से जन्म लेते हैं और उद्दण्ड तथा हिंसक बनते हैं। सगर के अश्वमेध करने पर घोड़ा लुप्त हो जाता है; पुत्र उसे खोजते हुए पृथ्वी खोदते हैं और ऋषि कपिल के पास उसे पाते हैं।","te":"సగరుని అరవై వేల మంది కుమారులు ఒక సొరకాయ నుండి పుట్టి ఉద్ధతులుగా, హింసాత్మకులుగా పెరుగుతారు. సగరుడు అశ్వమేధం చేస్తుండగా గుర్రం మాయమవుతుంది; కుమారులు దాని కోసం భూమిని తవ్వి కపిల మహర్షి దగ్గర దానిని చూస్తారు.","ta":"ஸகரனின் அறுபதாயிரம் மைந்தர்கள் ஒரு சுரைக்காயிலிருந்து பிறந்து முரடர்களாக வளர்கிறார்கள். ஸகரன் அஶ்வமேதம் செய்யும்போது குதிரை மறைய, மைந்தர்கள் அதைத் தேடிப் பூமியைத் தோண்டி கபில முனிவர் அருகே காண்கிறார்கள்.","ml":"സഗരന്റെ അറുപതിനായിരം പുത്രന്മാർ ഒരു ചുരയ്ക്കയിൽനിന്ന് ജനിക്കുന്നു; അവർ വളർന്നത് കാട്ടാളന്മാരായും ക്രൂരന്മാരായുമാണ്. സഗരൻ അശ്വമേധയാഗം നടത്തുമ്പോൾ കുതിര അപ്രത്യക്ഷമാകുന്നു; പുത്രന്മാർ അതിനെ തിരഞ്ഞ് ഭൂമി കുഴിച്ചുനോക്കുന്നു, കപിലമുനിയുടെ സമീപം അത് കണ്ടെത്തുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.105; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"तीर्थयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Tirthayatra Parva (The pilgrimage)","verses":[{"text":"लोमश उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Lomasha said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एतच्छ्रुत्वान्तरिक्षाच्च स राजा राजसत्तम ।\nयथोक्तं तच्चकाराथ श्रद्दधद्भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this from the sky, that best of kings, believing it, did as he was told, best of Bharatas."}},{"n":2,"text":"षष्टिः पुत्रसहस्राणि तस्याप्रतिमतेजसः ।\nरुद्रप्रसादाद्राजर्षेः समजायन्त पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sixty thousand sons of matchless splendour were born to that royal sage by Rudra's grace, king."}},{"n":3,"text":"ते घोराः क्रूरकर्माण आकाशपरिसर्पिणः ।\nबहुत्वाच्चावजानन्तः सर्वाँल्लोकान्सहामरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They were fierce and cruel in deed, roaming the sky, and in their great numbers they scorned all the worlds with their immortals."}},{"n":4,"text":"त्रिदशांश्चाप्यबाधन्त तथा गन्धर्वराक्षसान् ।\nसर्वाणि चैव भूतानि शूराः समरशालिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brave and fond of battle, they also harassed the gods, gandharvas and rakshasas, and all beings."}},{"n":5,"text":"वध्यमानास्ततो लोकाः सागरैर्मन्दबुद्धिभिः ।\nब्रह्माणं शरणं जग्मुः सहिताः सर्वदैवतैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Harassed by the foolish sons of Sagara, the worlds went with all the gods to Brahma for refuge."}},{"n":6,"text":"तानुवाच महाभागः सर्वलोकपितामहः ।\nगच्छध्वं त्रिदशाः सर्वे लोकैः सार्धं यथागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The fortunate grandfather of all the worlds said to them: \"Gods, go back with the worlds as you came."}},{"n":7,"text":"नातिदीर्घेण कालेन सागराणां क्षयो महान् ।\nभविष्यति महाघोरः स्वकृतैः कर्मभिः सुराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Before long a great and terrible destruction of the Sagaras will come about, gods, through their own deeds.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"एवमुक्तास्ततो देवा लोकाश्च मनुजेश्वर ।\nपितामहमनुज्ञाप्य विप्रजग्मुर्यथागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, the gods and the worlds, lord of men, took leave of the Grandfather and went back as they had come."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततः काले बहुतिथे व्यतीते भरतर्षभ ।\nदीक्षितः सगरो राजा हयमेधेन वीर्यवान् ।\nतस्याश्वो व्यचरद्भूमिं पुत्रैः सुपरिरक्षितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, after a good many days had passed, best of Bharatas, the mighty King Sagara was consecrated for a horse sacrifice, and his horse roamed the earth well guarded by his sons."}},{"n":10,"text":"समुद्रं स समासाद्य निस्तोयं भीमदर्शनम् ।\nरक्ष्यमाणः प्रयत्नेन तत्रैवान्तरधीयत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arriving at the dreadful sight of the waterless sea, though carefully guarded, it vanished right there."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततस्ते सागरास्तात हृतं मत्वा हयोत्तमम् ।\nआगम्य पितुराचख्युरदृश्यं तुरगं हृतम् ।\nतेनोक्ता दिक्षु सर्वासु सर्वे मार्गत वाजिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, dear one, the Sagaras, thinking the splendid horse stolen, came to their father and told him that the horse had been taken invisibly. He told them all to search for the horse in every direction."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततस्ते पितुराज्ञाय दिक्षु सर्वासु तं हयम् ।\nअमार्गन्त महाराज सर्वं च पृथिवीतलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, having their father's order, they searched for that horse in all the quarters, great king, and over the whole surface of the earth."}},{"n":13,"text":"ततस्ते सागराः सर्वे समुपेत्य परस्परम् ।\nनाध्यगच्छन्त तुरगमश्वहर्तारमेव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all the Sagaras came together, but found neither the horse nor the horse-thief."}},{"n":14,"text":"आगम्य पितरं चोचुस्ततः प्राञ्जलयोऽग्रतः ।\nससमुद्रवनद्वीपा सनदीनदकन्दरा ।\nसपर्वतवनोद्देशा निखिलेन मही नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"They came to their father and said before him with joined hands: \"King, the whole earth, with its seas, forests and islands, its rivers, streams and caves, its mountains and wooded regions,"}},{"n":15,"text":"अस्माभिर्विचिता राजञ्शासनात्तव पार्थिव ।\nन चाश्वमधिगच्छामो नाश्वहर्तारमेव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"has been searched by us on your command, but we find neither the horse nor its thief.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"श्रुत्वा तु वचनं तेषां स राजा क्रोधमूर्छितः ।\nउवाच वचनं सर्वांस्तदा दैववशान्नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing them, the king, stunned with anger and driven by fate, said to them all:"}},{"n":17,"text":"अनागमाय गच्छध्वं भूयो मार्गत वाजिनम् ।\nयज्ञियं तं विना ह्यश्वं नागन्तव्यं हि पुत्रकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Go, and do not come back; search again for the horse. Without that sacrificial horse you must not return, my sons.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"प्रतिगृह्य तु संदेशं ततस्ते सगरात्मजाः ।\nभूय एव महीं कृत्स्नां विचेतुमुपचक्रमुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking the order, the sons of Sagara again began to search the whole earth."}},{"n":19,"text":"अथापश्यन्त ते वीराः पृथिवीमवदारिताम् ।\nसमासाद्य बिलं तच्च खनन्तः सगरात्मजाः ।\nकुद्दालैर्ह्रेषुकैश्चैव समुद्रमखनंस्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then those heroes saw a split in the earth, and reaching that hole the Sagaras dug, and dug the sea with mattocks and with sharp spades."}},{"n":20,"text":"स खन्यमानः सहितैः सागरैर्वरुणालयः ।\nअगच्छत्परमामार्तिं दार्यमाणः समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dug by the united Sagaras, Varuna's abode fell into the deepest distress, being torn open all around."}},{"n":21,"text":"असुरोरगरक्षांसि सत्त्वानि विविधानि च ।\nआर्तनादमकुर्वन्त वध्यमानानि सागरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Asuras, serpents, rakshasas and many kinds of creatures cried out in agony as the Sagaras killed them."}},{"n":22,"text":"छिन्नशीर्षा विदेहाश्च भिन्नजान्वस्थिमस्तकाः ।\nप्राणिनः समदृश्यन्त शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Creatures were seen by hundreds and thousands with heads cut off, without bodies, with knees, bones and skulls shattered."}},{"n":23,"text":"एवं हि खनतां तेषां समुद्रं मकरालयम् ।\nव्यतीतः सुमहान्कालो न चाश्वः समदृश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they dug the sea, home of sea monsters, a great deal of time passed, and still the horse was not seen."}},{"n":24,"text":"ततः पूर्वोत्तरे देशे समुद्रस्य महीपते ।\nविदार्य पातालमथ संक्रुद्धाः सगरात्मजाः ।\nअपश्यन्त हयं तत्र विचरन्तं महीतले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, in the north-east of the sea, king, the enraged sons of Sagara split open the nether world and saw the horse roaming there on the ground."}},{"n":25,"text":"कपिलं च महात्मानं तेजोराशिमनुत्तमम् ।\nतपसा दीप्यमानं तं ज्वालाभिरिव पावकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They saw also the great-souled Kapila, a peerless mass of radiance, blazing with austerity like a fire with its flames."}}]}]}